{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfmmqaacP9jnR5ywxPzW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fit gives Dq ≈ 427 cm⁻¹ (so Δt ≈ 4270 cm⁻¹) and B ≈ 899 cm⁻¹. C is not determined by these bands.\n\n**Approach.** A tetrahedral d⁸ ion has a ³T₁(F) ground term. Its three spin-allowed bands are ³T₁(F)→³T₂, ³T₁(F)→³A₂ and ³T₁(F)→³T₁(P). The energy diagram has the same form as that of octahedral d², so I fitted the bands with the d² model.\n\n**Result.** The fit reproduces the three bands to within 2 cm⁻¹ (RMSE about 1.2 cm⁻¹):\n\n| Band | Observed (cm⁻¹) | Fitted (cm⁻¹) | Assignment |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ν₁ | 3 600 | 3 598 | ³T₁→³T₂ |\n| ν₂ | 7 870 | 7 871 | ³T₁→³A₂ |\n| ν₃ | 16 410 | 16 410 | ³T₁→³T₁(P) |\n\n**Checks.**\n- **Dq.** The splitting ν₂ − ν₁ equals 10Dq, which gives 4 270 cm⁻¹ and so Dq ≈ 427 cm⁻¹. This matches the fit.\n- **B.** B ≈ 899 cm⁻¹ is about 0.88 of the free-ion value for Ni²⁺ (roughly 1 040 cm⁻¹), which is a reasonable degree of covalency.\n- **C.** The fit used a default C of 3 801 cm⁻¹. These spin-allowed bands do not depend on C, so I am not reporting it as a result.\n\n{\"Dq\": 427, \"B\": 899, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Three spin-allowed bands of tetrahedral d8 were fitted with the equivalent d2 energy diagram, giving Dq and B; C is not constrained by these bands.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3594,"cache_read_input_tokens":7975,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3594,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cf515be1-5986-4d2c-b7be-33dda4cdefc5","uuid":"d15a91c0-7ac2-4fe8-8df4-bf35ffb98d21","timestamp":"2026-11-03T09:39:41.569Z","request_i